<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferryland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferryland is a town on the east coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avalon-peninsula">Avalon Peninsula</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. In 1621 George Calvert, later Lord Baltimore, founded the Colony of Avalon there, which he visited in person in 1627 and 1628 before turning to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>. Later held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Kirke, it is now a major archaeological site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferryland.jpg" alt="Ferryland" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: shankaronline (Flickr) · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferryland_Sign.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
